<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!-- FILING DEADLINES — seeded, effective-dated, and NOT YET VERIFIED.

         `noupdate="1"` so an upgrade never rewrites a rule an accountant has
         corrected. That is the whole reason these are records and not
         constants: the first person to check them against a current Ministry
         of Revenues schedule must be able to fix them in the UI, and their fix
         must survive the next release.

         WHAT 30 DAYS IS BASED ON. CLAUDE.md records, accountant-verified in
         July 2026: "pension via POESSA declaration + bank slip within 30
         days". VAT and withholding are given the same window BY ANALOGY, which
         is not the same as being verified. Their rows below carry the word
         UNVERIFIED and the exact question that would settle each one.

         EMPLOYMENT INCOME TAX IS NO LONGER ONE OF THEM. Its window is VERIFIED
         in docs/ethiopian-tax-reference.md section 2 — the return is filed
         "during the following Ethiopian month" — so its row uses the
         end_of_next_period shape rather than a day count. The two agree for
         every ordinary Ethiopian month, which is 30 days, and part at Pagume,
         which is 5 or 6: Nehase 2018's return is due 10 Sep 2026, where
         "+30 days" says 5 Oct.

         The effective date is 2000-01-01 rather than today's date on purpose:
         a rule that started this morning would make every historical period
         read "deadline unknown", and the page would be blank on exactly the
         data an operator wants to look at first.
    -->
    <data noupdate="1">
        <record id="deadline_vat" model="sapian.filing.deadline">
            <field name="filing_key">vat</field>
            <field name="effective_from" eval="'2000-01-01'"/>
            <field name="window">days</field>
            <field name="days_after_period_end">30</field>
            <field name="source_note">UNVERIFIED — by analogy with the pension window, which is not evidence. QUESTION: which article of Proclamation 1341/2024 or Regulation 570/2025 sets the VAT return deadline, and what does the etax.mor.gov.et VAT screen show?</field>
        </record>
        <record id="deadline_wht" model="sapian.filing.deadline">
            <field name="filing_key">wht</field>
            <field name="effective_from" eval="'2000-01-01'"/>
            <field name="window">days</field>
            <field name="days_after_period_end">30</field>
            <field name="source_note">UNVERIFIED — by analogy with the pension window, which is not evidence. QUESTION: which article of Proclamation 979/2016 as amended by 1395/2025 sets the withholding remittance deadline, and what does the etax.mor.gov.et withholding screen show?</field>
        </record>
        <record id="deadline_paye" model="sapian.filing.deadline">
            <field name="filing_key">paye</field>
            <field name="effective_from" eval="'2000-01-01'"/>
            <field name="window">end_of_next_period</field>
            <field name="days_after_period_end">0</field>
            <field name="source_note">VERIFIED — docs/ethiopian-tax-reference.md section 2: the declaration for one Ethiopian month is filed at any time during the following Ethiopian month. Accountant: "Sene taxes must be reported from Hamle 01 to Hamle 30." PwC: "by the end of the month following the month the income was earned."</field>
        </record>
        <record id="deadline_pension" model="sapian.filing.deadline">
            <field name="filing_key">pension</field>
            <field name="effective_from" eval="'2000-01-01'"/>
            <field name="window">days</field>
            <field name="days_after_period_end">30</field>
            <field name="source_note">CLAUDE.md, accountant-verified Jul 2026: POESSA declaration + bank slip within 30 days.</field>
        </record>
    </data>
</odoo>
